# Build outputs
dist/
Standalone/Build/
Engine/Build/
External/Assimp/Build/
External/Bullet/Build/

# Host-compiled intermediate .o files under External/. The Bullet/Assimp
# Linux Makefiles wildcard-glob these into the .so link (see
# Engine/Makefile_Linux BULLET_OFILES). COPY preserves mtimes so container
# make treats stale host .o's as up-to-date and skips rebuild. If the host
# ran a newer toolchain (e.g. Ubuntu 24.04 GCC 13 / glibc 2.39) the .o's
# reference symbols that don't exist in Bookworm (__isoc23_strtoll,
# std::ios_base_library_init) and the editor exe link fails.
External/Bullet/Intermediate/
External/Assimp/Intermediate/

# Stale host build artifacts under External/ — the container regenerates
# these from source (Dockerfile runs prebuild_libgit2.sh, make -C
# External/Lua, etc). A leftover CMakeCache.txt from a host build points
# at the host's source path (e.g. /home/uai/...), and cmake aborts the
# in-container prebuild with:
#   "The current CMakeCache.txt directory ... is different than the
#    directory ... where CMakeCache.txt was created"
Engine/External/libgit2/build/
External/Lua/*.o
External/Lua/liblua.a
**/CMakeCache.txt
**/CMakeFiles/

# Intermediate files
Standalone/Intermediate/
Engine/Intermediate/

# Git
.git/
.gitignore

# IDE
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# Docker (avoid recursive copy)
Docker/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs and temp files
*.log
*.tmp
